# clinical v1.16 — WARNING. A document status outside the ten-code set.
#
# "in-progress" is the realistic wrong value: it is a genuine FHIR code, on
# Task.status and Procedure.status, and it is what a converter writes when it
# maps a workflow state onto a document without checking which value set the
# document's own status is bound to. It is in neither composition-status nor
# diagnostic-report-status, so it is out of set under the wider binding and
# under the narrower one alike -- which means this fixture keeps meaning what it
# means if the ratchet later narrows clinical:ClinicalDocumentShape to
# composition-status for the DocumentReference-derived subtypes.
#
# sh:Warning, not sh:Violation, per the core v3.5 ratchet: existing pods already
# carry clinical:status and v1.16 is the first release to bind its value, so a
# value is reported and never rejected. See the sibling
# status-vitalsign-completed.WARN.ttl for why `.WARN.` is the only filename that
# states this claim correctly.
#
# clinical:documentReferenceStatus is left VALID here on purpose. The two status
# axes are independent, and a fixture that broke both would not show which one
# the warning came from.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:d0c00116-0000-4000-8000-000000000003> a clinical:ClinicalDocument ;
    clinical:displayName "Discharge Instructions" ;
    clinical:documentDate "2031-03-07"^^xsd:date ;
    clinical:status "in-progress" ;
    clinical:documentReferenceStatus "current" ;
    clinical:fhirResourceId "DocumentReference/dr-55990" ;
    clinical:fhirResourceType "DocumentReference" ;
    clinical:importedAt "2031-03-09T08:12:44-05:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
